P10-01 / P10-02 implementation
- Added Java-compatible Push settings, validation, TAG subscription entry points, concurrent/orderly listener contracts, offset-store selection, runtime registration and startup rollback. Orderly startup is rejected until Phase 12; real queue assignment and pull activation remain pending.
- Started the bounded concurrent-consume worker owner after offset-store load and before registration. Startup failures stop/join it before unregistering/shutting down; normal shutdown quiesces it before offset persistence and unregister.
- Added a startup fault point after worker startup and tests for all eight startup stages. The lifecycle test verifies the default 20 workers start, namespaced subscriptions and retry-topic subscriptions reach heartbeat data, and workers are gone after shutdown.
- The first worker shutdown test exposed a double-poll of completed Tokio `JoinHandle`s. The shutdown path now awaits the handle only after timeout/abort; the focused test passes.
- Checks passed: `cargo fmt --check`; `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked` (36 unit, 12 integration, 0 doc tests failed); `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`.
