P10-04 bounded pull scheduler foundation
- Added one owned due-time scheduler worker to Push startup, startup rollback and shutdown. Its pending work is keyed by queue plus assignment generation and coalesces to one scheduled/in-flight request with at most one follow-up.
- Added immediate/delayed scheduling, pause/resume, cancellation, stale-generation rejection, Java count/MiB/span threshold calculation, delayed-pull/backlog tracing, and Java-confirmed retry-delay constants. No pull response handling or fixed-assignment production API is claimed here.
- Added paused-time tests for coalescing, single follow-up, pause/resume, cancellation, stale generation, flow-control inputs and worker start/stop. Push lifecycle tests now confirm the worker starts once, stops on shutdown, and startup fault injection includes the scheduler stage.
- Checks passed: `cargo fmt --all`; `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer push::pull_service::tests --offline` (5 passed); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer push::consumer::tests --offline` (5 passed). The interim build emits expected dead-code warnings for PullRequest/flow-control functions that P10-05 will attach; strict Clippy is deferred until the pipeline uses them.
- Matrix status: PullRequest/PullMessageService P10-04/08 PARTIAL; P10-V02 PARTIAL pending outcome retry and send-back retention; P10-V04 startup lifecycle PARTIAL pending callback shutdown. P10-V03 remains PENDING_PHASE_19.

P10-05 bounded Push pull pipeline
- Wired private queue activation/removal to the due-time scheduler with assignment generations, suspend/resume handling, retry fencing while OFFSET_ILLEGAL correction is pending, and namespace/group validation before activation side effects.
- Added bounded pull RPC workers so broker long polls do not occupy the shared runtime pull-dispatch worker. Pull requests now resolve broker routes, build namespace-aware headers, read clustering commit offsets, invoke the typed pull RPC, decode/filter through the Phase 8 wrapper, and remove message namespaces before caching.
- Implemented queue pressure, paused, stale-generation and subscription checks; FOUND insertion/reschedule, safe NO_NEW/NO_MATCHED offset correction, OFFSET_ILLEGAL drop/freeze/persist/removal/rebalance flow, and Java-sourced 20ms/50ms/1s/3s delay selection.
- Added tests for pull outcomes, safe tag-offset correction, stale responses, OFFSET_ILLEGAL fencing and RPC retry-delay classification. P10-V03 remains `PENDING_PHASE_19`; real queue allocation remains owned by Phase 11 and consume submission is P10-06.
- Checks passed: `cargo fmt --check`; `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --offline` (50 unit, 12 integration, 0 doc tests failed); `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-targets --all-features --offline -- -D warnings`.
