P10-06 / P10-07 concurrent consume and retry
- Added bounded consume submission, concurrent listener execution with timeout/panic isolation, Java ackIndex handling, clustering send-back, retry-topic fallback and local redelivery when both retry paths fail. Broadcasting failures are discarded under Java semantics.
- Added fixture-backed success, partial, missing-status, panic, retry fallback/failure, broadcasting and private fixed-assignment coverage. The fixed assignment stays crate-private; retry fallback checks namespace composition and Java retry metadata.
- Pinned Java 5.5.1 inspection confirmed send-back uses the VIP channel, a fixed 5000 ms timeout, and the current message ID. Rust now matches these details. The Java reference checkout, including its pre-existing untracked file, was not modified.

P10-09 shutdown
- Shutdown stops pull/consume submission, drops assigned queue generations, cancels their scheduled pulls, waits within the configured budget, aborts a slow listener without committing it, persists offsets and joins owned tasks.
- The slow-listener test verifies cached/in-flight messages and the persisted offset remain unresolved while scheduler, RPC and consume worker counts return to zero.

